      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have the same issue without stations and without synced variables, just a gameObject with a rigidbody. While moving its transform.position visually gives the desired result for 1 frame, all the physics seems to ignore the new position and the gamObject stick to its previous position the next frame. I noticed that its only affecting some UdonBehaviour even if they share the same code.\n\nEdit: TimeScale seems to have a direct impact on how often the issue occurs\n\nEdit 2: Turning the UdonSharpBehaviour into regular C# MonoBehaviour script gives the same issue, s̶o̶ ̶i̶t̶ ̶i̶s̶ ̶p̶r̶o̶b̶a̶b̶l̶y̶ ̶a̶ ̶b̶u̶g̶ ̶w̶i̶t̶h̶ ̶U̶n̶i̶t̶y̶ ̶2̶0̶2̶2̶.̶3̶.̶6̶f̶1̶ ̶r̶a̶t̶h̶e̶r̶ ̶t̶h̶a̶n̶ ̶V̶R̶C̶S̶D̶K̶\n\nhttps://youtu.be/Fk3bHXqGC1E",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
