  "details": "This is oddly specific and hard to pin down but here is what I have observed:\n\nI'm having a bug in ClientSim for SDK 3.5.0 where the cars in my world aren't properly teleporting to their starting locations when you enter them. It works fine if I build and test the world in VRC and in ClientSim 3.4.1 for Unity 2019.\n\nWhether relevant or not, the cars are initially hidden GameObjects with stations, you are sent to them via a menu that enables them, waits a few frames then sends you to their seat, entering the seat runs code to put them in the right location but for some reason that isn't happening, or rather maybe it is but they are then sent back to their initial locations that they were at in the Unity editor.\n\nEven manually running the method in ClientSim that just teleports the car won't work although it reads the debug line fine:\n\n    public void CarToStartingLine()\n\n    {\n\n        car.transform.SetPositionAndRotation(spawnLocation.defaultSpawns[carNumber].position, spawnLocation.defaultSpawns[carNumber].rotation);\n\n        Debug.Log(\"resetCar bool is \" + resetState.resetCar + \" & Player Car \" + carNumber + \" sent to default spawn location \" + carNumber);\n\n    }\n\nIf you look at the attached movie, you can see that the car is initially in the right place then gets sent back to its default spawn location. I don't have any code telling it to respawn and it will move back to wherever its initial position is in the Unity Editor:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1WjsgEAExdXH1kVGDBMHwt4SHyCUzxqgA/view?usp=sharing\n\nRunning that method to teleport it doesn't seem to do anything from that point even though that's the method that was just used to send it to that location for that initial frame.\n\nI've been trying to get this to consistently not happen for a while now and I've hit about 10 false positives. Even stuff like disabling every line of code in a method except for the one that teleports the car to the track seems to work initially. I will then try re-enabling the rest of the code until it stops teleporting, but then disabling it all again except for the line that teleports the car suddenly also doesn't work?\n\nI have a feeling it's maybe something to do with stations or maybe ownership, but it's really hard to tell.\n\nThis is it working just fine in ClientSim for SDK 3.4.1 both when the method runs normally at the start of the race and every time I try to manually call it using ClientSim:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1UecMojvGW7GoFiAuoaxGhOrViY4122WS/view?usp=sharing",
